course: dictionary
lesson: 16128
title: Sound words in context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound like the noise they name. Whirr is one of them: say it aloud and you can hear a soft, steady buzz. «The fan began to whirr on the hot afternoon.» The word fan tells you what is making the sound, and the sound is a soft buzz, not a bang.
explain: Context also helps with the meaning of whirr when it is used for thinking. «My mind was whirring with ideas all night.» Minds cannot make a buzzing noise, so the sentence is saying something different: thoughts were spinning fast, as if they could not stop.
explain: Ask yourself what fits. Fans, cameras, wheels and wings can all whirr, because they all spin or move quickly. Then test your meaning in the sentence: a soft, steady buzz should still make sense in «the whirr of the fan».
fact: Whirr is a sound word, so say it aloud to hear the noise it names.
fact: Whirr can be a verb («The fan whirrs») or a noun («the whirr of the fan»).
fact: In American English the spelling is whir, without the second r.
fact: «Whirring» describes something spinning fast with a soft, steady buzzing sound.
fact: «My mind was whirring» means thoughts were spinning fast, as if they could not stop.
exercise: «The fan began to whirr on the hot afternoon.» What does whirr mean here? | *A soft, steady buzzing sound | A sudden silence | A loud crash | A bright flash of light
exercise: «We heard the whirr of the camera as it zoomed in.» What does the whirr mean? | *The soft, steady sound of the camera | The picture the camera took | The lens cap that fell off | The sound of a door shutting
exercise: «My mind was whirring with ideas all night.» What does this suggest? | She had lost her way | She was counting to ten | Her hair was blowing in the wind | *Her thoughts were spinning fast
test: «The wings of the hummingbird whirr as it hovers.» What does whirr mean? | *To make a fast, steady buzzing sound | To fall gently to the ground | To stand still in complete silence | To shout loudly across a field
test: Which spelling is the American English version of whirr? | *whir | wherr | whurr | wirr
exam: «The old machine whirred into life.» What does whirred mean? | *Made a fast, steady buzzing sound as it started | Broke into pieces with a bang | Fell asleep in the corner | Went quiet and still
